// Points that no scheme's public documents offer and a collective on FORA
// does. They are a list, not table rows.
const ADDS = [
  { title: 'A record of every fetch that the payer didn\'t produce.', text: 'In the six schemes that say how use is counted, the AI company reports its own use, the operator or the licensee counts it, or no one counts per use. CCC and CLA haven\'t said for AI. On FORA, every fetch is a transaction for one URL. The operator\'s Exchange, the marketplace that lists members\' content, signs the offer, and the AI company signs its acceptance.' },
  { title: 'Reports checked against the records, every period.', text: 'The schemes\' public terms offer at most an audit or a dispute right. On FORA, the operator reconciles each AI company\'s report with the fetch records before it splits the pool.' },
  { title: 'A share you can recompute.', text: 'Seven of the eight don\'t publish enough to redo the sum. GPT-NL publishes its rule; its public documents don\'t say whether a contributor gets the token counts and quality scores the sum needs. On FORA, your statement gives your weight, the total weight, the pool, the operator\'s cut and the version of the rule.' },
